'' A STATIC MEMBER IS NOT A STATIC LOCAL. 'static x as integer' inside a type is one
'' object for the whole program, named after the TYPE -- measured, '_ZN1T8COUNTER$E',
'' the ordinary nested-name mangling with the member component uppercased and a '$'
'' appended. tiko-lang named it the static-LOCAL way, '_ZN1T2S1Ev$x': whichever member
'' function first touched it. Within one translation unit the values were right;
'' across two the name would not agree.
''
'' The DEFINITION -- 'dim shared T.x as integer = 2' -- kept only its last component,
'' so with a module-level 'x' beside the type it found THAT one and quietly became a
'' second initialiser for the shared x. Measured: fbc gives the shared x the 1 it was
'' written with and '_ZN1T2X$E' the 2.
''
'' 'NS.U.val' needed one more thing: a namespace-qualified TYPE NAME had no type of
'' its own, so the member access above it had no base to look a field up in.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/static-member.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: global var i64 _ZN1T8COUNTER$E = 2
'' EXPECT-OUT: global var i64 _ZN2NS1U4VAL$E = 5
'' GOLDEN: expected/static-member.out
